## 1. Executive Summary

MedSync Health is committed to integrating environmental, social, and governance (ESG) principles into our core operations. The 2024 fiscal year marked a period of significant growth, with total revenue reaching **AED 485,100,000** and our global team expanding to **1,200 employees**. This report details our performance across key sustainability metrics, focusing on our operational footprint, social impact, and governance structure. Our primary focus remains on reducing our Scope 3 emissions, particularly those related to cloud computing and business travel, which constitute the largest portion of our environmental impact.

## 2. Environmental Performance: Carbon Footprint (FY 2024)

MedSync Health follows the Greenhouse Gas (GHG) Protocol for calculating our carbon footprint, measured in tonnes of Carbon Dioxide Equivalent (tCO2e). As a technology company, our emissions are predominantly categorized as Scope 3.

### 2.1. Total GHG Emissions by Scope

| Scope | Description | FY 2024 Emissions (tCO2e) | Percentage of Total |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Scope 1** | Direct Emissions (e.g., company vehicles, on-site fuel) | 15 | 0.3% |
| **Scope 2** | Indirect Emissions (Purchased Electricity) | 1,285 | 24.7% |
| **Scope 3** | Other Indirect Emissions (e.g., Cloud, Travel, Commuting) | 3,900 | 75.0% |
| **Total Emissions** | | **5,200** | **100.0%** |

**Carbon Intensity:** Our carbon intensity for FY 2024 was **10.7 tCO2e per AED 1 Million in Revenue** (5,200 tCO2e / 485.1 Million AED).

