### 2.3. IT Infrastructure and Cloud Emissions

Our IT infrastructure is a significant source of Scope 3 emissions. We maintain a hybrid environment, with the vast majority of compute operations hosted on cloud services.

| Metric | Value | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Total Employees** | 1,200 | (Source: Master Data Model) |
| **On-Premise Servers** | 50 | Used for legacy systems and specialized testing environments. |
| **Cloud Compute Percentage** | 95% | Primary provider is AWS (See SEC-005 for cloud security policy). |
| **Cloud Emissions (Scope 3)** | 1,500 tCO2e | Calculated based on usage data provided by AWS. |
| **Business Travel Emissions (Scope 3)** | 1,800 tCO2e | Primarily air travel for Sales and Executive teams. |

**Mitigation Strategy:** We are actively participating in the **AWS Healthcare Accelerator** program (a key milestone from June 2022) to optimize our cloud architecture for energy efficiency and are exploring carbon-neutral data center options.

